t where the fire  was raging just a few days ago and you  can see  the destruction left by the flames now  many buildings many homes like this one  there  right behind me have completely  burned out i can still smell the smoke  in the air almost the entire village has  been turned  into ashes now many people here  were brought elsewhere or went elsewhere  to stay there overnight so right now the  village is pretty much  deserted they told me they were able to  save their own lives  but they lost their livelihoods because  many people here in the area are farmers  they lost their fields their crops their  animals it's all gone  and now let's look a little further to  this direction this is the local mosque  it's also been  damaged by the fire now it's being used  to  organize aid people are collecting water  bread and clothing so the most necessary  items  to help people out now according to the  authorities more than a hundred  separate fires erupted in recent days  here in southern turkey and in western  turkey at the aegean coast  the vast majority of them they say are  now under control but a few are still  raging  so the firefighting operations continue  here in antarctica province as well  a wild wide-reaching wildfire with the  devastating effects uh president erdogan  has  visited the affected region facing a lot  of criticism  what more can you tell us about that  well yes he was here yesterday to  inspect the damages he  again promised quick help he said the  government would cover the rents of  people  affected and would rebuild their homes  as soon as possible  he also rejected criticism that had  emerged particularly on social media  concerning his government's  crisis management people were saying  that the authorities did not react  fast enough that they did not have the  proper equipment to get the situation  under control now erdogan said  that the number of firefighting planes  for example  had been increased recently from 6 to  13.  he said turkey 