eople question if the  climate has  become more chaotic what are your  thoughts  certainly what we're seeing is a rise in  extremes this is something that doesn't  always manifest in the way  that you might intuit it does uh from a  warming planet so  uh for instance more water and more  moisture is stored in the  atmosphere when temperatures rise which  leads to greater rainfall and uh more  intense flooding events  this manifests differently all across  the world and of course it manifests  differently according to  local factors as well but unfortunately  what we are seeing  is that the consequences of adding  greenhouse gases into the atmosphere  are resulting in a more chaotic as you  say atmosphere  uh and it's something again that was  predicted in general but unfortunately  these extremes  are perhaps somewhat worse than than was  predicted  the goal set out in the paris climate  accord is to cap  global warming at 1.5 degrees how  important  is it for this goal to be achieved  sooner rather than later and  is this really likely  when it comes to the emissions  reductions that need to be achieved  to reach a certain temperature goal what  is really  really important is that the bulk of  emissions reductions actually need to  occur  sooner rather than later and that is  because  uh the total quantity of greenhouse  gases that you add to the atmosphere  results in worse warming which basically  means the later we leave it  the worse the consequences even if we do  achieve say a net zero by 2050 target  across the world  uh if we do it sooner then the  consequences will be less bad  those disasters that you mentioned will  hypothetically be less severe or which  is of course something that we want  as to the feasibility of it i think it  is certainly  very very feasible it's something that  can be done uh there's something  what we see across the world is that  countries that really  put their mind to it and put effort into  it and achieving far more than was  